@startuml HostAndroidADB
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how an sbx agent drives an Android emulator on the host — host adb server, dialled by IP, one allowed port, artemis as the MCP driver
' covers: internal/hostadb/hostadb.go
' covers: internal/hostadb/hostadb_test.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go (addonAndroid, addonIOS, interfaceOptions, gateAddons, addonAliases)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (startHostADB)
' covers: internal/run/topology.go (interfaceOf)
' covers: internal/run/host_adb_test.go
' covers: internal/manifest/manifest.go (capabilities.hostDevices)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Spec allow)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/host_adb_test.go
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_host_adb_env, proveo_artemis_mcp_config)
' covers: internal/contract/host_adb_lib_test.go
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh (CLAUDE_MCP_ARGS)
' covers: defs/claudecode/harness.manifest (capabilities.hostDevices)
'   why this shape, measured ............ _spec/_experiments/mobile-device-reach.puml
'   the pattern it copies ............... _spec/internal/sbx/host-browser-cdp.puml
'
' ── WHY (2026-09-29) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' google/artemis drives Android through an adb SERVER it does not own
' (ADB_HOST/ADB_PORT). The box has no /dev/kvm, so the emulator lives on the
' host; the host adb server is the one seam a fresh VM can use without the
' host's adbkey (the emulator's adbd refuses a fresh key, measured).
'
' ── capabilities.hostDevices SELECTS THE ROWS ──────────────────────────────
'   android → addonAndroid  live under sbx; greyed without it
'   ios     → addonIOS      always greyed: "coming soon" (no artemis driver)
' `--addon android` resolves; `--addon ios` is refused with the same reason.
'
' ── HOST SIDE (internal/hostadb) ───────────────────────────────────────────
'   port    PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT, default 5037; Kit allow += localhost:<port>.
'   reuse   any serial the server lists in state "device" is reused as is.
'   launch  else `adb -P <port> start-server`, then `emulator -avd <avd>`
'           windowed, own process group, ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT=<port>,
'           left open after the run. Wait: host:devices + sys.boot_completed=1.
'   avd     PROVEO_HOST_AVD when it names an AVD, else the first listed.
'   sdk     ANDROID_HOME > ANDROID_SDK_ROOT > ~/Library/Android/sdk (darwin)
'           > ~/Android/Sdk; each tool falls back to PATH.
'
' ── GUEST SIDE (entrypoint lib) ────────────────────────────────────────────
'   proveo_host_adb_env        ADB_HOST=<ip> ADB_PORT=<port>
'                              ADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:<ip>:<port> (plain adb)
'   proveo_artemis_mcp_config  `uv tool install` artemis @ PROVEO_ARTEMIS_REF
'                              into the toolchain home (synced to the host),
'                              reinstalls only when the receipt lacks the ref,
'                              prints an mcpServers JSON for that python.
' After a fresh install opencv-python is swapped for opencv-python-headless
' at the same version: the GUI wheel links libxcb.so.1, which no proveo image
' ships, and `python -m mcp_server` dies importing cv2 without the swap.
' Measured in a guest (uv 0.9.26, arm64): install 733 s, 985 MB tool env;
' swap 89 s; initialize answered in 3 s by artemis 1.30.0, logging
' "Activated remote ADB server endpoint 169.254.1.1:5037".
' claudecode passes it as `--mcp-config <json>`: per launch, never
' `claude mcp add --scope user`, which would land in the mounted home.
'
' ── WHAT THE AGENT CAN DO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' ADB is full control of every device on that server. The server also dials:
' host:connect opens a TCP socket FROM THE HOST, outside sbx egress, and the
' emulator's own traffic leaves through the host's network. The run warns so.
' A relay that forwards only device services is the deferred fix
' (mobile-device-reach.puml).
' [Unverified] whether sbx enforces the Kit allow on the direct path; the
' host's global policy was allow-all during every measurement.

actor "Operator" as OP
node "host" as HOST {
  component "proveo run" as RUN
  component "adb server\n127.0.0.1:5037" as ADB
  component "Android emulator\nwindowed AVD" as EMU
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM {
  component "claudecode\n--mcp-config artemis" as AG
  component "artemis MCP\nADB_HOST=169.254.1.1" as ART
}

OP --> EMU : watches, logs in once
RUN --> ADB : start-server
RUN --> EMU : reuse or boot
RUN --> VM : Kit allow localhost:5037\nenv PROVEO_HOST_ADB_PORT
AG --> ART : stdio MCP
ART --> ADB : adb protocol by IP
ADB --> EMU : emulator-5554

note right of ADB
  **The server is the seam.** A fresh VM key
  reads unauthorized on adbd :5555; the server
  holds the host key and answers the VM, so
  the key never leaves the host.
end note

note right of ART
  **Installed once, pinned.** uv installs the
  pinned ref into the toolchain home, which
  syncs to the host; a later run reuses it
  unless the receipt names another ref.
end note
@enduml
